Fix graph-tool imports when built without Cairo support.

When graph-tool is configured with --disable-cairo, importing graph_tool.draw.cairo_draw fails to import
symbols from the unavailable Cairo drawing library. The ImportError is currently caught and converted to a warning,
after which the module continues initialization and attempts to use undefined symbols such as vertex_attrs,
resulting in a NameError.

Re-raise the original ImportError after issuing the warning. This allows graph_tool.all to treat the drawing module as
unavailable optional functionality and continue loading the remaining graph-tool functionality,
as required for headless graph-tool-base installations.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT5.6
--- a/src/graph_tool/draw/cairo_draw.py
+++ b/src/graph_tool/draw/cairo_draw.py
@@ -82,1 +82,2 @@
     warnings.warn(msg, RuntimeWarning)
+    raise
